y without hitting anything, which implies the use of echolocation.\n- Echolocation is a biological sonar system used by bats and dolphins to navigate and locate objects in their environment by emitting high-frequency sounds.\n- These sounds are beyond the range of human hearing and are beyond the range of most other animals.\n- When the bat emits these sounds, they bounce off objects in its environment and return to the bat as echoes.\n- The bat uses its large ears to detect these echoes, which allows it to build a mental map of its surroundings and avoid obstacles.", "new_cot_probs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0], "cot_prob": [-106.0], "cot_step_prob": [-81.5]}}}
